          </div>
        </div>

        <!-- Closing CTA -->
        <div class="mt-16 bg-gray-900 text-white rounded-2xl p-8">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            <strong class="text-white">Carpet is fine with a dense rubber mat, a
            monthly vacuum and a hood clean twice a year.</strong> On deep pile or
            foam underlay, add a rigid board under the mat — a frame that is not
            sitting flat is the reason a belt will not stay centred, and no roller
            adjustment fixes it.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed">
            Re-level at two weeks, when the carpet has finished settling. If the
            belt is already wandering, work through
            <a href="/how-to-center-treadmill-belt/" class="text-[#5AA9FF] font-bold no-underline">centring the belt</a>,
            and keep the rest of the machine on the
            <a href="/treadmill-maintenance/" class="text-[#5AA9FF] font-bold no-underline">maintenance schedule</a>.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </article>
